thag2.47:1.1 starts: Coming into the conceit of delight, the mind
thag2.47:1.2 starts: impales itself on a stake.
thag2.47:1.3 starts: Wherever’s a stake, a chopping block,
thag2.47:1.4 starts: there, only there, you turn.
thag3.15:1.1 starts: Whoever wants to do later
thag3.15:1.2 starts: what he should have done first,
thag3.15:1.3 starts: falls away from the easeful state
thag3.15:1.4 starts: & later repents.
thag2.36:2.1 starts: My mind, standing like rock,
thag2.36:2.2 starts: doesn’t shake,
thag2.36:2.3 starts: dispassionate for things that spark passion,
thag2.36:2.4 starts: unprovoked by things that spark provocation.
thag2.36:2.5 starts: When my mind is developed like this,
thag2.36:2.6 starts: from where can there come to me
thag2.37:1.1 starts: It’s not for sleeping,
thag2.37:1.2 starts: the night garlanded
thag2.37:1.3 starts: The night, for one who knows,
thag2.37:1.4 starts: is for staying awake.
thag3.9:2.1 starts: Touched by gnats
thag3.9:2.2 starts: in the wilds,
thag3.9:2.3 starts: like an elephant
thag3.9:2.4 starts: He, mindful,
thag3.10:2.1 starts: For I’ve seen that faith is inconstant,
thag3.10:2.2 starts: wavering.
thag3.10:2.3 starts: Even they who are passionate
thag3.10:2.4 starts: Why should a sage waste away over
thag4.2:3.1 starts: Apt attention arose in me,
thag4.2:3.2 starts: the drawbacks appeared,
thag4.2:3.3 starts: disenchantment stood
thag4.2:3.4 starts: at an even keel:
thag4.4:1.1 starts: A curse on bodies—
thag4.4:1.2 starts: full of foul smells,
thag4.4:1.3 starts: siding with Māra,
thag4.4:1.4 starts: where nine streams are always flowing.
thag4.4:4.1 starts: Whereas those dispassionate for
thag4.4:4.2 starts: passion,
thag4.4:4.3 starts: don’t delight there,
thag4.4:4.4 starts: have cut the cord,
thag4.8:1.1 starts: In both ways
thag4.8:1.2 starts: I’m known as Rāhula
thag4.8:1.3 starts: because I’m the son of the Buddha,
thag4.8:1.4 starts: because I’ve the eye that sees Dhammas,
thag5.1:1.1 starts: I, a monk,
thag5.1:1.2 starts: saw a woman cast away,
thag5.1:1.3 starts: discarded
thag5.1:1.4 starts: there in the cemetery.
thag5.1:4.1 starts: Then apt attention arose in me,
thag5.1:4.2 starts: the drawbacks appeared,
thag5.1:4.3 starts: disenchantment stood
thag5.1:4.4 starts: at an even keel:
